Async single-database configuration.

The connection URL is not in alembic.ini. env.py builds it from
app.core.config.Settings, the same object the application connects with, so
there is one definition of "which database" and no password in a tracked file.

    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add filings"   # writes a draft
    uv run alembic upgrade head
    uv run alembic downgrade -1

Autogenerate is a draft, not an answer. It does not see generated columns,
native enum changes, partitions or materialised views, it renders a renamed
column as a drop plus an add, and it will propose dropping anything it does not
understand. Read every generated file, and write the downgrade yourself.

The rules this directory has to keep (one head, dated filenames in chain order,
a real downgrade on every revision after the baseline) are asserted in
tests/test_migrations.py.
